{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 102, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing the direct input-to-output edge leaves only edge 4 as the path to the output, so the accuracy loss is much larger (exp 5)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a weak pooling op on edge 0 frees the cell from a harmful early bottleneck, whereas removing a conv deletes useful capacity (exp 15)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on edge 2 with a parameter-free skip discards learned capacity and hurts much more than replacing pool or none (exp 9)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the conv on the edge feeding the output for pooling removes important capacity, which is worse than swapping out a skip or none."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is none, node 2 never reaches the output, so upgrading edge 1 into node 2 yields little gain (exp 6)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 5 is none, edge 2 feeds a dead node, so adding a conv there cannot improve the output."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 0 is none, node 1 receives no input, so a conv on edge 4 out of node 1 contributes little (exp 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a harmful pooling op on the final edge with a 3x3 conv gives a larger gain than replacing a skip or a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Upgrading an existing 1x1 conv to a 3x3 gives only a marginal gain compared with replacing skip, pool or none with a conv (compare exp 20 with exp 13)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Deleting a pooling shortcut on edge 3 loses little, while deleting a conv or skip on that edge removes a valuable path to the output (exp 8)."}], "tok": 8864, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [3, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none"], [1, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [3, "none"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [2, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "skip_connect"], [5, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_conne